      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now let me check the compile script and working directory.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has serious compilation issues: `E` used as a raw type without declaration, method stubs without bodies (`__super_makeEmptyIterator()`, `__super_makeObject()`), and dead code. I'll write a clean, understandable version that preserves only the `testBounded()` behavior.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all dead/non-compilable code (unbound `E` type parameter, method stubs without bodies, unused helper methods), uses `String` throughout, and adds a class-level Javadoc comment explaining the test scenario (offset=2, max=4 on a 7-element list yields \"c\",\"d\",\"e\",\"f\") to make the intent immediately clear."
